[Intro]

[Verse 1]
[00:31.33]We found her in the morning by the nine grey stones
[00:35.51]Her staff had taken root where it did stand
[00:39.92]The salt was gone, the cloak of crow had melted into earth
[00:44.01]And the moss came soft and green about her hand

[00:48.47]We did not lift her, we did not weep aloud
[00:52.74]We did not name her, for her name was paid
[00:57.04]We knelt about the ring as one might kneel before a hearth
[01:01.41]And we listened to the sound the river made

[Pre-Chorus]
[01:05.82]Sól aftr komin
[01:10.12]Vár, vár, vár

[Chorus]
[01:14.61]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[01:18.19]Thou hast heard us in the end
[01:22.56]Thou hast taken what was offered
[01:26.54]Thou hast given back the wind
[01:31.56]Várkoma, várkoma
[01:35.28]Where the green doth rise again
[01:39.55]Where the long white hush is broken
[01:43.73]By a small and patient rain

[Verse 2]
[01:48.97]The children came who had not seen a summer in their lives
[01:52.79]We took them to the river by the hand
[01:56.86]We showed them how the ice doth speak before it letteth go
[02:01.31]We showed them how the buds do understand

[02:05.48]The old ones lit no fire, for the air was warming on its own
[02:09.89]The smith laid down the hammer he could lift
[02:14.10]The priest of the new god, he wept and would not say for what
[02:18.15]And the wood received his tears as it received the gift

[Pre-Chorus]
[02:22.94]Sól aftr komin
[02:27.12]Vár, vár, vár

[Chorus]
[02:31.60]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[02:35.21]Thou hast heard us in the end
[02:39.77]Thou hast taken what was offered
[02:43.75]Thou hast given back the wind
[02:48.78]Várkoma, várkoma
[02:52.67]Where the green doth rise again
[02:56.63]Where the long white hush is broken
[03:00.92]By a small and patient rain

[Bridge]
[03:05.80]We buildeth no cairn where she lay
[03:09.94]We buildeth no stone, we buildeth no name
[03:14.15]The moss is her marker, the moss is her song
[03:18.22]And the moss shall remember when we shall be gone

[03:22.91]She is the green now
[03:24.94]She is the breath
[03:27.03]She is the spring that was bought with a death

[Final Chorus]
[03:31.57]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[03:35.26]Thou hast heard us in the end
[03:39.71]Thou hast taken what was offered
[03:43.69]Thou hast given back the wind
[03:48.51]Várkoma, várkoma
[03:52.36]Where the green doth rise again
[03:56.76]Where the long white hush is broken
[04:00.82]By a small and patient rain

[Outro]
[04:06.19]Vér erum heim komin
[04:14.45]Vér erum heim komin
